{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1143647-alternate-unseelie-legacies","id":1143647,"title":"Alternate Unseelie Legacies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-24T20:04:34-07:00","id":1143647,"title":"Alternate Unseelie Legacies","content":"I like that C20 has clarified that Seelie doesn't mean &quot;good&quot; and Unseelie doesn't mean &quot;evil&quot;. The description of the courts is pretty clear on this, and portrays unseelie as more individualistic than traditional. However, when you get to Legacies, it does seem to be pretty clearly good vs. evil. Most of the unseelie legacies seem to be what most people would consider &quot;bad&quot;. Despite my two decades of experience with this game, I'm just now creating an unseelie character that I want to be more &quot;good&quot;, but very much individual and against most traditional court structures. He is going to be a pretty nice guy, and dashing, but very much his own person. Yet when going through the legacies, I'm having a hard time finding something that fits, when all of the unseelie ones are brutal, criminal, or otherwise fairly horrible. These legacies do seem to support Unseelie=Bad and Seelie=Good, which they shouldn't.<br /> <br /> How have the rest of you gotten around this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T22:48:45-07:00","id":1143680,"title":"","content":"Personally I do not see most Unseelie legacies as &quot;bad&quot; but rather samewhat selfish and self centered which leads to more individualistit general demeanor. <br /> <br /> For a generally nice guy, dashing and still his own person perhaps Peacock. Afterall they aren't too bad just a bit childish at times, but in that way they are quite similar, and in my opinion no more bad or childish than Dandy Seelie legacy.<br /> <br /> Only Beast, Grotesque, Outlaw and Savage are actually something that could be considered &quot;bad&quot;. And even most of these can be played, while still remaining true to the quest and ban, in a non &quot;bad&quot; manner, the only one who remains more or less bad is the Savage as people tend to think anyone actively rejecting civilized manners as &quot;bad&quot;. But mostly, though the descriptions are slanted towards &quot;bad&quot; behaviour, you can remain true to the Unseelie quests and bans without being a bad person though you will generally be more self centered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T04:44:49-07:00","id":1143735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1143647-alternate-unseelie-legacies#post1143647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that C20 has clarified that Seelie doesn't mean &quot;good&quot; and Unseelie doesn't mean &quot;evil&quot;. The description of the courts is pretty clear on this, and portrays unseelie as more individualistic than traditional. However, when you get to Legacies, it does seem to be pretty clearly good vs. evil. Most of the unseelie legacies seem to be what most people would consider &quot;bad&quot;. Despite my two decades of experience with this game, I'm just now creating an unseelie character that I want to be more &quot;good&quot;, but very much individual and against most traditional court structures. He is going to be a pretty nice guy, and dashing, but very much his own person. Yet when going through the legacies, I'm having a hard time finding something that fits, when all of the unseelie ones are brutal, criminal, or otherwise fairly horrible. These legacies do seem to support Unseelie=Bad and Seelie=Good, which they shouldn't.<br /> <br /> How have the rest of you gotten around this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had similar feelings. To deal with it without revisiting everything, I tried to treat UnLegacies as &quot;as darker &amp; endgier&quot;, reasoning, that among other things, Unseelie have stronger affinity with darker impulses of humanity, but because of that they have much better handle of those dark impulses and can focus them better into constructive, healthy direction. Something, their Seelie brothers and sisters might find harder.<br /> <br /> We can cover Unseelie Legacies (and their Seelie Counterparts) case by case basis, here, reworking archtypes and bans or just the wording, if it would be enough.<br /> <br /> If you want Individualistic/Reformationist versus Community-oriented/Traditionalist, than you should incorporate it in both sets of Legacies.<br /> <br /> One, potentially good way to do this (I think)... is to make one set of Legacies, common for all Court/Arias, with a single ban and two paragraphs for Seelie and Unseelie specific differences. Of course, you'd need to write more, if you'd need to expand on Adhene Arias/Inaniamae Courts/etc. But it can be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 09-25-2017, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T06:19:25-07:00","id":1143753,"title":"","content":"2nd edition was the same in that aspect. It stated that seelie doesn't equal good and unseelie doesn't equal evil, but the legacies clearly didn't back that up.<br /> <br /> IMO the problem isn't so much that the Unseelie Legacies are inherently bad but more that they are presented as selfish and asshole-ish, but they can definitely be interpreted in a more positive light (the inverse being true for Seelie legacies as well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","user":"Sinister Spider","date":".  Fixing typos 09-25-2017, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T07:07:24-07:00","id":1143771,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that in C20 you can now ignore your primary legacy's ban by using your secondary legacy. When I was playtesting, that seemed to go a long way to tempering the extremes legacies can get to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T10:27:57-07:00","id":1143837,"title":"","content":"I think in a perfect world instead of legacies the behaviour would be based on the Unseelie/Seelie Codes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T19:35:23-07:00","id":1143947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1143647-alternate-unseelie-legacies?p=1143771#post1143771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that in C20 you can now ignore your primary legacy's ban by using your secondary legacy. When I was playtesting, that seemed to go a long way to tempering the extremes legacies can get to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll have to go back and find that, as I don't remember it. That would definitely help mitigate some of the &quot;bad&quot; stuff about the Unseelie Legacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T21:08:10-07:00","id":1143961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1143647-alternate-unseelie-legacies?p=1143680#post1143680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only Beast, Grotesque, Outlaw and Savage are actually something that could be considered &quot;bad&quot;. And even most of these can be played, while still remaining true to the quest and ban, in a non &quot;bad&quot; manner, the only one who remains more or less bad is the Savage as people tend to think anyone actively rejecting civilized manners as &quot;bad&quot;. But mostly, though the descriptions are slanted towards &quot;bad&quot; behaviour, you can remain true to the Unseelie quests and bans without being a bad person though you will generally be more self centered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast: Any Shonen protagonist who's obssessed with being &quot;the best&quot; in a field(like.. Goku from Dragonball)<br /> Grotesque: Your edgier comedians, or trickster figures, honestly how much of this I'd say is defined by what its secondary legacy combines with.<br /> Outlaw: I&quot;m just going to point out captain Jack Sparrow.. just because you put yourself first doesn't mean you can't bring your friends along.<br /> Savage: this is very dependent on what people consider &quot;natural&quot; Wild and civilized. I can imagine this Legacy has all sorts of fun debates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T22:54:44-07:00","id":1143980,"title":"","content":"Like said they are generally the ones portrayed as worst and like I mentioned, and now Lian offered examples, even they can be played as non &quot;bad&quot;. The rest of the Unseelie legacies are even easier to play in a non-Evil/bad way. Yes the fluff teet on them is written with the worst examples in mind but otherwise the Unseelie legacies are fine as they are, the quests and bans do not force one in any way to be a bad person especially since now one can situationally ignore ones ban as mentioned by PookaKnight.<br /> <br /> So again in my opinion theres nothing wrong with the legacies but obviously YMMV or we wouldnt be having this conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T11:49:08-07:00","id":1146115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sinister Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1143647-alternate-unseelie-legacies?p=1143753#post1143753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2nd edition was the same in that aspect. It stated that seelie doesn't equal good and unseelie doesn't equal evil, but the legacies clearly didn't back that up.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's sort of an artifact of the 1st ed. One of the things about all of WW's 2nd eds back in the day is that they all came out two years after the 1st (like clock work, with Vampire, coming after only about a year, being the exception). And part of this is that a lot of 1st ed stuff just got reprinted verbatim, even if it didn't quite fit other changes that were made. If there's been a revised ed of Changeling back around the turn of the millennium, you probably would've seen the legacies overhauled a bit. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T15:32:32-07:00","id":1146463,"title":"","content":"The weird thing I find about legacies and the intersection of courts is that they are both Political factions AND moral impulses. I kind of want some way to separate the two. Noble and just champions of Freedom and Chaos and Tyrant lords imposing their wills on others...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T19:20:56-07:00","id":1146525,"title":"","content":"There is a brief note in C20 that it\u2019s possible to follow one Court\u2019s Legacy while attempting to uphold the code of the opposing Court. <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think it\u2019d be easy or at all common, but it is explicitly possible to treat Legacy and Court as separate affiliations - one innate and one political.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T19:29:12-07:00","id":1146528,"title":"","content":"Whats Ranma's suppressed unseelie legacy if I could ask? Peacock? <br /> <br /> Or Haseo (From Dot Hack GU)s suppressed seelie, and active unseelie legacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T19:39:37-07:00","id":1146533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1143647-alternate-unseelie-legacies?p=1146525#post1146525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a brief note in C20 that it\u2019s possible to follow one Court\u2019s Legacy while attempting to uphold the code of the opposing Court.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think it\u2019d be easy or at all common, but it is explicitly possible to treat Legacy and Court as separate affiliations - one innate and one political.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I COULD easily see a Unseelie Gwydion Ringleader say Upholding ideals of the Seelie Court or at least pushing it politically. I could easily see a Seelie Legacy Ailil fighting for the ideals of the Unseelie court, but that's very much their house basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}